This image is shaped like a cross with curved ends, except the top is open. It has two sides in the middle which are connected by curves at the end. The straight lines are light green and have black dots throughout. Where it is straight, there are lines connecting the dots on each side. Starting on the left top, it begins with 5’. At the first curve is U in a box followed by a dot. Around the curved left side, it begins with A in a pink box followed by a dot, followed by Pu in a pink box. Following this is a dot followed by G [superscripted star], then G in a pink box, then A in a pink box then a dot. Below this, it states, “Contains two or three D residues at different positions.” This entire curve is labeled as D arm. In the bottom point curve, it begins with Py in a pink box, then U. Following this is a U-shaped yellow box lined in black with three dots. This is labeled as wobble position. Below this is a bracket with 5’ on the left and 3’on the right and labeled as anticodon. Following this a pink box with Pu, followed by a dot. This entire curve is labeled as anticodon arm. Where the bottom and right straight lines curve right, there is a dip down and right with green circles, and is labeled as an extra arm variable in size, not present in all tRNAs. On the right curve, it begins with G in a pink box, followed by T in a pink box, then [psi] in a pink box, then C in a pink box. This is followed by 4 dots, then C in a pink box. This entire curve is labeled as T[psi]C arm. At the top on the right is a pink box going upward that meets the end of the green section. From bottom to top, it has Pu, C, C, A inside and labeled as the amino acid arm. Above this is 3’. 

